{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 12 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D7"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the rocuronium bromide shortage on 2023-02-15 and lists multiple manufacturers as Current, including Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA, Inc. and Hospira, Inc.",
      "cites": ["E44", "E36", "E37"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hikma product used at Corvale sites is manufactured at HIKMA FARMACEUTICA (PORTUGAL), S.A. (FEI 3002807173), a registered plant whose last inspection was VAI on 2023-04-21.",
      "cites": ["E17", "E15"]
    },
    {
      "text": "That plant received a VAI classification on 2023-02-03, which was 12 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2023-02-15.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "An earlier inspection of the same plant ended 2020-03-06 with a VAI classification, 1076 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["D6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hospira, Inc. (FEI 1021343) is an approved alternate manufacturer with a registered plant last inspected NAI on 2025-02-07.",
      "cites": ["E31", "E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 7.1 days of 10 mg/mL 5 mL vials on hand, Corvale Lakeside has 28.5 days, and Corvale General has 19.2 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked option is to transfer 13 vials of 10 mg/mL 5 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East to 9 days while leaving Corvale Lakeside with 15 days.",
      "cites": ["D10"]
    }
  ]
}
